    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Will Smith** leads the charge with an elite 67.88 rating. Facing the 4.71 xERA of Lodolo, **Will Smith** benefits from a strong #3 order position and favorable park factors, making him our highest-confidence start. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** is close behind at 66.69; while he faces a slightly tougher matchup in Newcomb, his high base projection and top-of-the-order usage keep him as a locked-in asset. We are also leaning into **Dylan Beavers**, who jumps to a 65.61 score thanks to his #1 slotting and a significant +7% platoon advantage against Tong. These three represent our primary offensive engine, with each player benefiting from optimized order placement or exploitable pitcher profiles.\n\nThe benching of **Braden Montgomery** remains the most notable decision of the day. Despite a solid base projection, his score dipped to 32.65 due to a stifling matchup against Williams, whose 2.89 xERA renders him an elite arm we cannot afford to gamble on given our strict game-cap management. We preferred the safer utility profile of **Kyle Karros**\u2014who enjoys a massive +14% park boost at Mize\u2019s expense\u2014over the downside risk of playing **Braden Montgomery** in a sub-40 environment. Elsewhere, we continue to monitor the status of **Cal Raleigh**, whose 54.47 score is contingent on confirmed lineup placement in the #4 hole. While **JJ Bleday** draws a difficult assignment against the formidable Skubal, his +14% dynamic platoon edge against the lefty keeps him in the lineup as a marginal start, provided he can navigate the difficult SP matchup. **Masyn Winn**, **Gleyber Torres**, and **Kyle Karros** round out the active roster, offering steady floors to support our core stars.",
